 Product Engineer 
Are you a technical expert with coaching skills and a passion for product management? Then this vacancy as Product Engineer at Efcon Water is exactly what you are looking for. 
Your impact 
In this role, you will have the opportunity to combine your technical expertise and coaching skills. As our Product Engineer, you will work closely with a team of technicians with the aim of providing our customers with the best products and thereby contributing to the growth of Efcon Water. In addition to supervising the team, you will also monitor the production process of our products. 
You will have the freedom to shape this position yourself and can count on the stability of a large organisation in the background. You will not only contribute to the technical development of our products, but also to the growth and development of Efcon Water B.V. 
Some of your responsibilities will include 
- Guiding a team of technicians; 
- Developing and monitoring the production process; 
- Setting up compliance strategies and drawing up Standard Operating Procedures (SOP); 
- Collaborating with marketing and contributing to product innovation. 
This is you 
- Higher professional education (HBO) degree in Electrical Engineering, or relevant work experience; 
- Experience in leadership and knowledge of Electrical Engineering; 
- Experience with programming PLC controllers; 
- Familiarity with Research & Development; 
- Strong communication skills in both Dutch and English. 
What we offer you 
- A salary range between €3,500 and €4,500 gross per month plus a profit-sharing/bonus scheme; 
- 25 days' holiday with the option to purchase additional days; 
- Nice extras for Easter, Sinterklaas and Christmas; 
- A good working atmosphere in an informal company; 
- Travel allowance and pension scheme; 
...

In line with our expectations, we expect our team members to be passionate about their work, to act with honesty and integrity, and to have a healthy dose of enthusiasm. The desired skills for the Quality Control Employee are also:
*  At least MBO level of working and thinking;
* 2-3 years work experience as a Quality Control Employee in a food company;
* Flexibility: working in four overlapping shifts, with Saturdays occasionally forming part of the working week;
* Fluency in spoken and written English; Dutch is an advantage;
* Knowledge of HACCP and GFSI;
* Strong communication skills, persuasive and decisive;
* Works accurately and is proactive;
* You are proficient in Excel and Word.

The New Plant - At The New Plant we produce Beyond Meats plant-based protein products for customers in Europe, the middle East and parts of Africa. Beyond Meat has been partnering with McDonalds sinds 2021 and supplies the vegetarian patty for the McPlant. Within your team, you will be working alongside three Quality Control Employee, a Quality Control Supervisor and a Quality Control Manager, and you will collaborate with two Quality Assurance Assistants.

Can your colleagues in production count on spotless and hygienic workspaces? Do you enjoy staying active on the job? Then you can quickly start working as a cleaner or industrial cleaner at Luiten! Your full-time workday starts around 9:00 or 10:00 AM. You’ll change into your work attire, grab your cleaning materials and equipment, and begin moving between the various production areas with your high-pressure cleaner.
Not only will you thoroughly clean the production spaces, but you’ll also ensure that the machines used to process and package meat—and all related materials—are meticulously cleaned. You take care of your own work, following HACCP and hygiene regulations carefully. In addition to cleaning, you make sure that every area is safe to enter and ready for use.
No need for an activity tracker here, as you’ll definitely get plenty of daily movement in this role! Together with your friendly, multicultural team, you’ll ensure production can start on time and in a clean environment.

- You are available full-time from Monday till Friday;
- Overtime doesn’t wear you out—instead, it makes your wallet fuller;
- You speak Dutch or English, essential for safety on the work floor;
- Some experience with cleaning and/or sanitation is a plus.

